  "files": {},
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Sliding windows bound attention and the KV cache",
    "description": "Sliding-window attention lets each token attend only to the latest w positions, giving O(nw) cost and a rolling cache of size w. Stacked layers extend the theoretical receptive field to about Lw, though information can dilute; global tokens can add document-level access."
  }
